  "body": "In the two-bank cross-shear interface, arbitrary invertible within-bank bridges and heterogeneous paid call ranks satisfy `sum(r_i) >= 2n + max(r_i)`. Thus a controller at the minimum `2P+1` stages, with `n=P*v` and every call rank at most `v`, must use full rank `v` in every call. This excludes one specific partial-rank boundary-stage shortcut; it is a structural research result, not a new supplier or kappa.\n\nThe field-independent proof credits PR743's diagonal-rank potential and adds an explicit cyclic endpoint-conjugation argument. Finite evidence fully covers GL(4,F2): 20,160 states, 604,800 edges and exact rank/call Pareto points `(3,6),(5,5)`. A separate dense rank-one BFS independently matches every weighted distance; all rank-two decompositions, rotation checks over F2/F3/F5, mathematical mutations and eight package controls pass, including optimized Python. Selected-record integrity and staged whitespace checks pass.\n\n```sh\npython -I -B research/stage-rank-rigidity41/verify.py\npython -I -B research/stage-rank-rigidity41/independent.py\npython -I -B research/stage-rank-rigidity41/test_package.py\n```\n\nRank is not identified with every geometry-dependent copied-center price. Extra connector banks, nonlinear messages, cross-bank bridges and partial exchanges are outside the theorem. No physical/native supplier replay, global invoice, cold/full suite, hosted CI or Lean execution is claimed.\n\nCredit 0xjohnnydev PR743, Jacob Sussman and the borrowing-controller lineage, PR397's indexed identity, and all pinned source contributors. Prepared for @woklerx with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0. Both implementations are AI-written, not independent human review.\n",
